  "body": "Release 0.20.0. This PR carries the release notes, the changelog rows, the gathered decisions and the version bump.\n\n**Start condition**\n\n- The cut started at 2026-11-14T17:57Z.\n- No `P1` or `P2` issue was open at that time.\n- The cut condition was the frozen list of 14 `P1`/`P2` issues that the maintainer set on 2026-11-14. All 14 are closed.\n\n**Cut fixes**\n\n- The local batch gate on main `4f4edcf35` was red: the post refused two legal stock-source hole cuts. Issue 1691 records it.\n- PR 1692 corrected it and merged as `058e14ca0`. This branch contains that merge.\n- The first local release gate on head `182b7018a` was red in the kernel suite `step_agreement`. The STEP bench read a file without a limit on truck's mesher, and the test did not end. Issue 1697 records it.\n- PR 1698 (issue 1697) corrected it and merged as `101d82f9d`. It is the second cut fix. This branch contains that merge. A new gate will run on the new head.\n\n**Gate**\n\n- The maintainer decided to run the release gate locally. The Linux cut runner has a defective compile cache (issue 1690), thus `cut.yml` is not used for this cut.\n- The first gate ran on head `182b7018a`. The new gate runs on the new head of this branch. The pixel-snapshot lanes run after it. A comment will give the result.\n- The tag is made by hand on the merge commit of this PR, after the check that the gated tree and the merged tree are the same.\n\n**Known issues**\n\n- None at this time. No `P1` or `P2` issue is open.\n\n**Not exercised**\n\n- No real control ran the changed post output. The release notes list the PRs.\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
